  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following set of quantum numbers.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">A</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">B</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">C</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">D</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>The number of correct sets of quantum numbers is</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For a given &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>&#39; value&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;will have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;values and for a given &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>&#39; value&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;will have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;values</p><p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;is not possible.Similarly for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;is also not possible,&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;have same values.</p><p>So, set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>&nbsp;are not possible.</p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;can have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;values and &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&#39; can have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;values,</p><p>So, set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;is possible.</p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>can</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>have</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>values</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>can</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>have</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>values</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>So, set C is also possible.</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;the correct set of quantum nmbers.</p>"
  }
